# Illustrative rule, not legal guidance.

rule sanctions.owned-by-listed v0.1
says "A vendor is BLOCKED if it carries an ACTIVE sanctions listing itself, or is owned, directly or through a chain of owners, by a party that does."

subject party

collection engagements : engagement for subject via vendor
collection ownerships  : ownership
collection listings    : listing

closure owned-by over ownerships from owned to owner

conclude Blocked when
  some engagement e in engagements
  some listing l in listings
  require e.vendor is-a l.party
  require l.list-status = active
